# Chaos: no other server's or client's name in what the player reads (Lua, OTUI, OTMOD, JSON; applies after 0001-0058).
# The base client kept names of its own project and of a server it came from in UI text. Now:
# - game_helper: the side-bar shortcut under the orb reads "Open Helper" (was another server's bot name), and the
#   helper's settings / save-data boxes say "Helper"; the click handler is onOpenHelperClick.
# - game_report: the name and statement report reasons say "the game" / "staff".
# - Cyclopedia magical archive spell texts and map marker labels (gamelib, game_realminimap, markers.json): our world.
# - client_entergame: the "Connection refused" box no longer points to another project's site.
# - the hidden stock top menu's Discord button no longer opens another server's invite (the link still comes from
#   Services.status, as before).
# - module descriptions (.otmod) and the game_memleak warning without the base client's name; .otmod author and
#   website lines (attribution) are kept.
# The removed lines still carry the old text: a diff has to name what it replaces (as in 0014).
# tools/ci/check_names.py --client <assembled tree> checks the result (client/BASE.md).
